<Layout title="SpinReel Privacy Policy" description="How SpinReel handles local photos, audio, projects, video exports and optional Google Play purchases.">
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy / SpinReel</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy — <em>SpinReel</em></h1>
    <p><strong>Effective date:</strong> November 8, 2026<br /><strong>Developer:</strong> Velvet &amp; Pixel<br /><strong>Contact:</strong> <a href="mailto:velvetandpixel@gmail.com">velvetandpixel@gmail.com</a></p>
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>SpinReel turns selected photos into roulette-style videos. Editing, audio mixing and rendering happen on your Android device. No Velvet &amp; Pixel account is required. We do not operate a server that receives your photos, audio, projects or finished videos.</p>
    <h2>Photos, audio and projects</h2>
    <p>Photos and audio you select are imported into private local working storage. Originals stay untouched. Project names, selected provider references, ordering, timing, audio settings, thumbnails and presets are stored on your device. Selected originals or provider references may contain metadata, including location information. Generated videos do not intentionally copy the original photos' location metadata.</p>
    <p>The app uses Android's system photo and document pickers rather than unrestricted access to your media library. A provider you choose may offer cloud services under its own privacy policy.</p>
    <h2>Free exports and Pro purchases</h2>
    <p>SpinReel provides three free successfully saved video exports with all editing features. Further exports require an optional one-time Pro purchase through Google Play. Editing, project settings and previews remain available after the free allowance is used. The app stores local export identifiers to count the allowance across projects and app updates. Failed or cancelled saves do not spend a free export. Saving or sharing an already completed export does not spend another allowance.</p>
    <p>Google processes payment through your Google Play account. SpinReel does not receive your card details. The app receives signed purchase proof and purchase tokens to verify ownership and acknowledge the purchase. It stores verified proof privately for offline Pro access. Purchase and allowance records are separate from project files and excluded from Android backup.</p>
    <p>Purchases, localized prices, restoration and online ownership checks use Google Play. A successful ownership refresh may remove refunded or revoked access. Previously verified Pro can remain available offline until an online refresh. Velvet &amp; Pixel does not operate a purchase-verification server. Google Play checkout availability depends on the installed build and the active store product.</p>
    <p>Clearing app storage or uninstalling removes local allowance and purchase records but does not cancel a completed Google Play purchase. Eligible purchases can be restored with the purchasing Google account. The free allowance is local to this installation; it is not an account-based usage history.</p>
    <h2>Google SDK technical information</h2>
    <p>SpinReel includes Google Play Billing and related Google SDKs. These SDKs can send operational and diagnostic information to Google, including app package/version, Billing SDK and Android versions, device manufacturer/model/build, language/country, network/carrier information, billing results and error codes, event timing and temporary billing-session identifiers. Communication can occur before a purchase, including initialization, price queries and ownership checks.</p>
    <p>Your photos, audio, projects and finished videos are not passed to the billing SDK. SDK events may be queued locally for later transmission. Google determines retention and processing on its services. Deleting a project or uninstalling does not delete information already held by Google.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's Privacy Policy</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://play.google.com/about/play-terms/">Google Play Terms of Service</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/retention">Google data retention information</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://myaccount.google.com/data-and-privacy">Google Account privacy controls</a></li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Advertising, analytics and diagnostics</h2>
    <p>SpinReel has no ads, subscriptions or developer-operated analytics/crash-reporting service. Google SDK operational diagnostics are described above. Export diagnostics and development device-check reports may include device/codec details, timing, errors and resource measurements. These reports stay local unless you choose to save or share them.</p>
    <h2>Saving and sharing</h2>
    <p>Completed videos are saved to your device through Android's media storage. You choose whether to share a video or diagnostic report and which destination receives it. Other apps or cloud-connected destinations process shared files under their own policies. Photos, exported videos and shared copies outside SpinReel remain until you remove them from their respective locations.</p>
    <h2>Retention, backup and deletion</h2>
    <p>Projects, imported working media, presets, appearance preferences and purchase-related local records remain on your device until removed or no longer needed. App-managed private data is excluded from Android cloud backup and device transfer. SpinReel does not provide cloud backup or synchronization.</p>
    <p>Deleting a project removes its saved project record; unused working assets are cleaned up on a best-effort basis. Media still referenced by other projects or presets is retained. Project deletion does not reset the free-export allowance or remove a Pro purchase. Temporary rendering/import files may remain for recovery or retry and are cleaned up by the app.</p>
    <p>Clearing app storage or uninstalling removes private projects, imported working media and local settings/records. Export videos you wish to keep first. Original media and videos saved outside the app are not deleted by uninstalling. Google-held payment and technical records are governed by Google's policies and controls.</p>
    <h2>Security and children</h2>
    <p>SpinReel uses Android's private storage and system mechanisms for media selection and sharing. Private storage controls access; the app does not add a separate encryption layer to project or receipt files. Purchase signatures verify authenticity rather than encrypting their contents. No software can guarantee absolute security.</p>
    <p>SpinReel is a general-purpose creative tool and is not specifically designed for children. We do not knowingly operate a service collecting children's personal information.</p>
    <h2>Policy updates and contact</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy when functionality or integrations change. The current effective date appears above. For privacy questions, contact <a href="mailto:velvetandpixel@gmail.com">velvetandpixel@gmail.com</a>.</p>
  </article>
